To determine how long the candy will last, we start by calculating the total number of pieces Emily has. She received 5 pieces from her neighbors and 13 pieces from her older sister. Adding these together:

$$
5 + 13 = 18
$$

Emily eats 9 pieces of candy each day. To find out how many days the candy will last, we divide the total number of pieces by the amount she eats per day:

$$
18 \div 9 = 2
$$

This means the candy will last Emily 2 days. The calculation checks out because $9 \times 2 = 18$, which is the total number of pieces she has.

