First, we need to determine the total number of trays Luke needs to carry. He has to pick up 20 trays from one table and 16 trays from another. So, the total number of trays is:

20 trays + 16 trays = 36 trays.

Next, we need to figure out how many trips Luke will have to make. Since he can carry 4 trays at a time, we divide the total number of trays by the number of trays he can carry per trip:

36 trays ÷ 4 trays per trip = 9 trips.

However, we must consider that if there are any trays left over after the division, Luke will need an additional trip. In this case, 36 divided by 4 is exactly 9, with no remainder. Therefore, Luke will make 9 trips in total.

So, the answer is 9.

